"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Park Joon-hyung, known professionally as Joon Park, is a South Korean-born American singer, rapper, actor and entertainer. As a singer, he is best known as the leader and rapper of the Korean pop group g.o.d.","title":"Joon Park","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joon_Park"}},"Q486634":{"id":"Q486634","name":"Jang Hyun-seung","ko":"장현승","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1989-09-03","death":"","birthplace":"Suncheon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2009","agencies":[{"name":"Cube Entertainment","id":"Q484449","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q269595","name":"Highlight","start":"2009","end":"2016"},{"id":"Q492416","name":"Trouble Maker","start":"2011","end":"2018"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/89_h/","x":"https://x.com/doublev89","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/0f7d7848-59b6-43c4-af92-b76b1a799628"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/Jang_Hyun-seung_at_V-Pop_Festival_Concert_on_January_2014_01_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jang_Hyun-seung_at_V-Pop_Festival_Concert_on_January_2014_01_(cropped).jpg","author":"Doolki","license":"CC BY 4.0"},"bio":{"text":"Jang Hyun-seung most often credited as Hyunseung, is a South Korean singer. He is best known as a former member of the boy group Beast. With Beast, he has released singles and albums in both Korean and Japanese. Beast won the Artist of the Year (Daesang) award at the Melon Music Awards in 2011. Hyunseung was also one half of the duo Trouble Maker with former Cube label mate, Hyuna. In December 2011, the duo released their debut extended play with eponymous lead single Trouble Maker. In October 2013, the duo released their second extended play, Chemistry, of which the title track \"Now\" was the first song to max out the score on music show Inkigayo with 11,000 points.","title":"Jang Hyun-seung","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jang_Hyun-seung"}},"Q496170":{"id":"Q496170","name":"Sandara Park","ko":"박산다라","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Dara","Sandy Park","Krung-krung","Darong"],"birth":"1984-11-12","death":"","birthplace":"Busan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","model","voice actor","rapper"],"debut":"2009","agencies":[{"name":"YG Entertainment","id":"Q50595","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Star Music","id":"Q4667782","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q171885","name":"2NE1","start":"2024","end":"2016"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/daraxxi/","x":"https://x.com/krungy21","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCX4uTPyZkp1d0ogkNNp8LtA","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/e8cfbf58-95cc-42f3-92e8-c616b66b02c0"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Sandara Park, also known mononymously as Dara (다라), is a South Korean singer, actress and television presenter. She rose to fame in the Philippines as a contestant on the ABS-CBN original talent show Star Circle Quest in 2004, after which she had a successful acting and singing career before returning to South Korea in 2007. She made her Korean debut in 2009 as a member of the K-pop group 2NE1, which became one of the most popular K-pop groups in the world. Park is one of the most recognizable Korean celebrities in the Philippines and is considered a leading figure in the spread of Korean wave into the country.","title":"Sandara Park","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sandara_Park"}},"Q496362":{"id":"Q496362","name":"Hwang Chansung","ko":"찬성","birthName":"황찬성","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Hwang Chan-sung"],"birth":"1990-02-11","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","film actor","television actor","actor","composer","rapper"],"debut":"2008","agencies":[{"name":"JYP Entertainment","id":"Q483238","start":